    source: https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=470
    notes: 'JCM 470 and DSMZ 792 describe the same fourteen named salt inputs and
      quantities in 1000 ml water, acidified to pH 1 with diluted sulfuric acid. JCM
      writes MnSO4·xH2O while DSMZ specifies the monohydrate; x is not established
      to differ from 1. This is compatible evidence with unresolved reagent hydration,
      not proof of different preparations. Source accessions and their occurrence
      routes remain separate provenance. The identifier is a conditional historical
      proposal handle; no winning owner, merge, simultaneous installation or complete
      component grounding is approved. Coordinator reconciliation under #1237 must
      preserve both source assertions, pH method and all inherited holds.'
